  "result": "The clone backend is in place and follows ADR 0012 where it disagrees with the product notes. Typecheck and the existing suite pass, and a throwaway smoke test of the clone (since removed) passed.\n\nNo visible test encoded behaviour this change alters, so none were edited.\n\nChoices the spec left open:\n\n- **Search, usage and audit are written directly by `cloneProject`**, not by new listeners on `project.cloned`, so they happen even when the event handlers aren't registered.\n- **Usage meters are incremented by delta** (one project plus the number of copies), the same way the existing listeners do it, rather than recounted.\n- **Webhooks**: `project.cloned` is not added to the subscribable webhook event types, since the task said nothing else changes.\n- **Key collisions**: a key already used in the workspace fails on the database's unique index when the project row is inserted, before any issue is written.\n- **Atomicity**: the issue copies go in as one transaction, but the project row is inserted before it and is not rolled back if that transaction fails.",
